playstation is defined by its exclusives  and that's especially true over its most  recent generations some of which are an  absolute necessity to play if you have a  ps4 or ps5 console so we put together a  list of 15 exclusives that should  absolutely  not be missed  sure the dark souls series is what  developer from software is most widely  known for but for anyone who's had a  good dose of bloodborne in their  bloodstream knows that that game is  possibly the studio's strongest title  it's like dark souls but gothic  terrifying vicious and  way more blood soaked no doubt that it's  just as difficult as the souls series  riddled with a haunting story  cryptically interlaced through its world  but bloodborne just hits different it's  way faster and way spookier it also has  this hot mama  it's a part of the ps plus collection so  if you haven't played it yet well then  maybe it's time that you learn to fear  the old blood  death stranding certainly has a unique  approach to open world game design one  that's spent walking around keeping your  balance climbing uneven terrain and  delivering packages it's hard to  understand its appeal at first glance  but at its roots it's a game about  connecting an america that's become  disbanded fractured and forced into  hiding due to a grave and commanding  threat it's a little too on the nose in  our post 2020 world but that makes it  all the more poignant and worth playing  today also you best believe it's as  off-kilter as you'd expect coming from  the mind of kojima the director's cut of  the game is coming out on september 24th  with updated visuals and new content  besides it also has norman ritas taking  care of a baby and drinking monster  energy drinks so yeah  okay yeah we already mentioned  bloodborne but we can't possibly ignore  the game that started it all demon souls  it's the game that put from software on  the map as the studio who would become  known for brutally challenging action  rpgs when it originally came out it was  more of a cult hit in comparison to the  later games in the series so it only  made sense to bring it back a decade  later as a launch game for the ps5 few  games showed off what the next  generation felt like as well as the  demon souls remake its textures lighting  load times and the use of the dual sets  are all remarkable remake studio blue  point games didn't change what made the  original masterpiece but instead  smoothed out the edges and presented the  modern classic as it should be seen  today  there has been a few game creation tools  released for consoles but none of them  have reached the heights of dreams  though dreams has a short campaign  created with in-game tools mind you and  it's really good the true star of the  show is the massive creation suite that  allows you to build pretty much whatever  you can think of from the ground up like  all tools it's kind of a learning curve  of course but the well of user made  creations is simply staggering and you  could easily spend hours upon hours  playing or watching other creators work  [Music]  after being announced only to slip back  into the shadows followed with multiple  delays and a complete revamping to its  design it's a surprise the final fantasy  remake even came out not to mention the  miraculous recapturing of the original's  essence but final fantasy remake does  more than just hone in on the magic of  the first but create something entirely  distinct that sets it as its own  marvelous adventure while it  controversially moved to real-time  combat the result paid off thanks to a  considered system that balanced strategy  over mindless hacking and slashing it  reimagined midgard in staggering detail  and emphasized its characters with more  depth than the original allowed the  result is a journey worth taking  regardless of whether you cared about  the first or not  ghost of sushima is the definitive  samurai game it's stitched together with  high noon drama scenic vistas stoic  heroes and  blood spray through and through it's a  love letter to classic samurai cinema  playing constant homage to the style of  films made legendary by director akira  kurosawa it has a beautiful open world  to explore or meditate with a spanning  combat system and some nice buns if you  haven't played this one give it a shot  it was recently released with a  director's cut with new content and  while you're at it you might as well go  give yo jimbo a watch you won't regret  it  [Music]  it's not often that a reboot of a  beloved franchise becomes the best game  in the series however sony santa  monica's god of war did well just that  it did more than just trade greek  mythology for norse it gives its leading  man some much needed depth and delivers  a story focused experience god of war  gives a new side to kratos one that's  more contemplative albeit still flawed  but more introspective especially with  the dynamic of his son atreus god of war  hands down has some of the best  cinematic action scenes ever made and is  layered with a thoughtful combat system  if you have a playstation 5 it has a  free upgrade that features 4k resolution  and 60 frames per second and is also a  part of the ps plus collection  [Music]  horizon zero dawn is one of the best  first party open world games for  playstation developer gorilla games  crafted a unique post-apocalyptic world  that feels both primitive and futuristic  and that's thanks to its robot dinosaurs  all of which is boasted thanks to a  great story with excellent combat that  involves studying a machine to figure  out the best approach to taking it down  the sequel horizon forbidden west is set  to release in february of 2022 for ps5  and ps4  the last of us was by many considered  the ps3's best game it was so damn good  and ended in such a way that the very  idea of a sequel was just controversial  it just didn't need one or so we thought  until the last of us part two came along  the whole thing is a meditation on  revenge and takes the time to see its  story of anguish and violence through  many different lenses the result is  something that is at times hard to  stomach and even uncomfortable and well  it's a topic that shouldn't be easy to  stomach in the first place it's combat  is a well-balanced ballet of action  violence and stealth which is  intricately packaged with a brilliantly  realistic world in heartbreaking  performances it's a display of naughty  dog's unflinching confidence and it  pushes the medium of games and  interactive storytelling in bold new  directions  [Music]  marvel's spider-man is easily one of the  best superhero games ever made swinging  through manhattan streets scoping out  its skylines from its highest points and  beating up baddies as spider-man has  never felt more spider-man like it's  also a great spidey story and an  incredibly well-written peter parker  it's follow-up spider-man miles morales  though a shorter adventure still  impresses thanks to the characterization  of miles morales the ps5 ultimate  edition includes marvel spider-man all  three expansions and the miles morales  campaign  bet you never saw this one coming  persona 5 royal is an expanded version  of one of the best jrpgs on ps4 but it's  more than a simple re-release with added  content it's got a whole bunch of new  stuff including a superb new palace  however most impressively is how it's  reworked its original content developer  atlas made sweeping changes to the  original story that helps it tie  together in a much more impactful and  meaningful way and regardless of whether  you're familiar with the persona  franchise or not this is a fresh start  so no context is needed to just jump in  and start stealing hearts the original  is available via ps plus collection but  we'd recommend opting for persona 5  royal if you can  [Music]  ratchet and clank rift apart is a  spectacle of the ps5's power its effects  environments low times are all turned up  to 11 including the dual sense haptic  feedback and adaptive triggers it's also  the introduction of rivet with a  storyline that interweaves alongside  ratchet giving two distinct gameplay  experiences including the new mechanic  of instantaneously transporting to holy  new environments and it's a whole bunch  of fun  [Music]  returnal takes the roguelike genre and  launches it into the aaa stratosphere  and beyond with the exception of the  game hades returnal is one of the few  games to take the roguelike formula and  infuse an engaging and thought-provoking  story throughout it it's also arguably  one of the most difficult games on this  list it uses the formula to deliver a  punishing experience that requires trial  and error to make progress with an  emphasis on dodging and nimble gun  gunplay it's one of the best ps5  exclusives but just be wary if you're  not a roguelike fan it may be hard to  get into  shadow of the colossus was one of the  best ps2 games in blue point games the  same studio behind the demon souls  remake brought it back in style with the  2018 remake just as it was 15 years ago  shadow the colossus is a towering feat  in storytelling and game design taking a  formula like zelda's dungeons and making  them physically walking towering colossi  that wander the world determining how to  topple the colossi is a part of the  mystery and requires more than just  platforming but puzzle solving and a bit  of ingenuity it's also just stunning to  look at and tells one gut punch of a  story  nathan drake swan's song brought naughty  dog's charming action adventure to a  fitting conclusion at least when it  comes to drake's arc uncharted 4 a  thief's end has more spacious set pieces  than early entries allowing for a more  free-form approach to exploration and  combat it feels less scripted than  drake's other adventures which in turn  provides a greater sense of discovery in  the adventure it's large in scope and it  balances its moving parts exceedingly  well to give a proper goodbye to one of  sony's most iconic characters you do  know that you're not actually nathan  drake you shut your mouth  you shut it it's a character i will cut  you i will open you up and bleed you out  and that wraps it up if you're a ps4 or  ps5 owner and haven't given any of these  a shot well consider taking the time to  squeeze it up on your backlog list  anyways thanks for watching and don't  forget to give us a thumbs if you liked  it and a sub for more gaming content  [Music]
 

